# Sahara Labs Validator Node Setup Guide

This guide will walk you through the process of setting up a validator node for the Sahara Labs network.

## Prerequisites

Before you begin, make sure your server meets the following system requirements:

- **CPU**: 4 vCPU cores
- **RAM**: 8 GB or more
- **Disk**: 100 GB SSD (recommended)
- **OS**: Ubuntu 20.04 or later (Linux)

## Step 1: Install Dependencies

### 1.1 Install Golang

Sahara Labs requires Go version 1.18 or higher. To install Go, run the following commands:

```bash
ver="1.18.6"
wget "https://golang.org/dl/go$ver.linux-amd64.tar.gz"
sudo rm -rf /usr/local/go
sudo tar -C /usr/local -xzf "go$ver.linux-amd64.tar.gz"
rm "go$ver.linux-amd64.tar.gz"
echo "export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/go/bin:$HOME/go/bin" >> $HOME/.bash_profile
source $HOME/.bash_profile
```

Verify the Go installation:

```bash
go version
```

### 1.2 Install Git and Other Dependencies

Make sure `git` and other required packages are installed:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install git build-essential curl jq -y
```

## Step 2: Clone the Sahara Labs Repository

1. Clone the Sahara Labs repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/saharalabs-io/sahara.git
cd sahara
```

2. Build and install the Sahara node:

```bash
make install
```

This will install the `sahara` binary.

## Step 3: Configure the Node

### 3.1 Set Configuration Options

Set the necessary configuration options for the node:

```bash
sahara config chain-id sahara-test-1
sahara config keyring-backend test
sahara config node tcp://localhost:26657
```

### 3.2 Initialize the Node

Initialize the node with your preferred moniker (replace `YOUR_PREFERRED_MONIKER` with your chosen name):

```bash
MONIKER="YOUR_PREFERRED_MONIKER"
sahara init $MONIKER --chain-id sahara-test-1
```

### 3.3 Download Genesis File

Download the genesis file and address book:

```bash
curl -Ls https://snapshots.kjnodes.com/sahara-testnet/genesis.json > $HOME/.sahara/config/genesis.json
curl -Ls https://snapshots.kjnodes.com/sahara-testnet/addrbook.json > $HOME/.sahara/config/addrbook.json
```

### 3.4 Add Seeds and Set Minimum Gas Prices

Modify the configuration file to add the seeds and set minimum gas prices:

```bash
sed -i -e "s|^seeds *=.*|seeds = \"3f472746f46493309650e5a033076689996c8881@sahara-testnet.rpc.kjnodes.com:26659\"|" $HOME/.sahara/config/config.toml
sed -i -e "s|^minimum-gas-prices *=.*|minimum-gas-prices = \"0.00001usahara\"|" $HOME/.sahara/config/app.toml
```

### 3.5 Set Pruning Options

Configure pruning to optimize the node’s performance:

```bash
sed -i -e "s|^pruning *=.*|pruning = \"custom\"|" $HOME/.sahara/config/app.toml
sed -i -e "s|^pruning-keep-recent *=.*|pruning-keep-recent = \"100\"|" $HOME/.sahara/config/app.toml
sed -i -e "s|^pruning-interval *=.*|pruning-interval = \"10\"|" $HOME/.sahara/config/app.toml
```

## Step 4: Download Latest Snapshot

To quickly synchronize your node, download the latest snapshot:

```bash
curl -L https://snapshots.kjnodes.com/sahara-testnet/snapshot_latest.tar.lz4 | tar -Ilz4 -xf - -C $HOME/.sahara
```

## Step 5: Start the Node

Start the Sahara Labs node as a service:

```bash
sudo systemctl start sahara.service
sudo journalctl -u sahara.service -f --no-hostname -o cat
```

Monitor the logs to ensure the node is running correctly.

## Step 6: Become a Validator

### 6.1 Create a Wallet

Create a wallet for your validator:

```bash
sahara keys add <wallet_name>
```

### 6.2 Generate the Validator's Public Key

Generate your validator’s public key:

```bash
sahara tendermint show-validator
```

### 6.3 Create the Validator

To create the validator, use the following command (replace the placeholders with your specific details):

```bash
sahara tx staking create-validator \
  --amount=<amount_tokens> \
  --pubkey=$(sahara tendermint show-validator) \
  --moniker="<validator_moniker>" \
  --chain-id=sahara-test-1 \
  --commission-rate=<commission_rate> \
  --commission-max-rate=<max_commission_rate> \
  --commission-max-change-rate=<max_commission_change_rate> \
  --min-self-delegation=<min_self_delegation> \
  --from=<wallet_name>
```

### 6.4 Confirm the Transaction

Confirm the transaction and wait for it to be included in the block.
